Domain context: read `context/*.md` only when the loop's typed `files_to_touch` event names the path. Usage rules: run the INDEX protocol yourself — Read `codegen/usage_rules/INDEX.md`, look up every dep you touch (cap 5), Read each cited file, fold the constraints into your implementation.

Read the pitch body at the top of your prompt → edit source → NEVER run builds → `mise exec -- npm install` for new deps only → edit the files in `## Declared Scope`, plus any sibling the sweep proves is required (justify each extra in your section body) — context/rules updates are curator's job post-reviewer → call `codegen-log section developer-static --slug <slug>` (stdin body — full CLI contract in session-log rules § Ownership) to write your section at canonical rank, AND `codegen-log append developer-static --files-modified @- --slug <slug>` (JSON array of the same relative paths from `## Files Modified`) — this typed event grants the reviewer's Read on any `context/*.md` you touched (`<slug>` = build slug from orchestrator). Done: source updated, log appended.

